# Camera dei Deputati — candidate votazioni for the "recent" scope mode.
# Endpoint: https://dati.camera.it/sparql
# License: CC BY 4.0
# Used by: tools/fetch_camera_votes.py (only when tools/config/votes_scope.json
# has "mode": "recent" — "explicit" mode skips this query entirely and uses
# the configured voteUris directly).
#
# Scope, all three explicit per docs/v2/04-votes-import.md's findings:
#   - Assemblea only (ocd:rif_assemblea bound) — in practice this is true for
#     essentially every ocd:votazione in this graph (no committee-level
#     "votazione" entities were found), but kept explicit as documentation
#     of intent, not just an accident of the data.
#   - "electronic" == non-secret (ocd:votazioneSegreta 0). Secret-ballot
#     votes exist in the graph but their per-deputy ocd:voto records only
#     carry the generic dc:type "Ha votato" (presence, not a disclosed
#     position) — genuinely un-attributable by design (ballot secrecy), not
#     a gap in our query. Including them would misleadingly imply we know
#     something we don't.
#   - XIX legislature only.
#
# fetch_camera_votes.py appends "LIMIT <n>" itself (n comes from
# tools/config/votes_scope.json, validated as a small positive integer
# before string interpolation) — there is no LIMIT in this file.
PREFIX ocd: <http://dati.camera.it/ocd/>
SELECT DISTINCT ?v ?date WHERE {
  ?v a ocd:votazione ;
     ocd:rif_leg <http://dati.camera.it/ocd/legislatura.rdf/repubblica_19> ;
     ocd:rif_assemblea ?assemblea ;
     ocd:votazioneSegreta 0 ;
     <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> ?date .
}
ORDER BY DESC(?date)
